"""j716-listen: curses TUI for the J716s speaker listening test (LISTENING-TEST.md).

Run as the desktop user (PipeWire session) in a terminal on the MacBook:

    j716-listen             the TUI
    j716-listen --check     print the environment and exit
    j716-listen --selftest  generate every signal, validate the WAV files, exit (plays nothing)

It generates the test signals itself (stdlib only, into ~/j716-listen/), plays them with
pw-play, steps the wpctl sink volume, watches speakersafetyd (journal) and dmesg for the
stop rules, and appends one Markdown row per play to ~/j716-listen/results.md.

Root is needed only for: reading dmesg and the speakersafetyd journal if the user is not
allowed to (the tool runs `sudo -v` once at start and then uses `sudo -n`), the
bring-up/profile switch (`sudo j716-audio-ab`), and, if plain amixer is refused, the
Speaker Switch toggle (`sudo amixer`).

J716_LISTEN_FAKE=1 swaps every system call for a simulator that plays nothing (also
J716_LISTEN_FAKE_TRIP=power|fault|restart|gain|stale, J716_LISTEN_FAKE_TRIP_AFTER=<s>).
J716_LISTEN_DIR overrides ~/j716-listen.
"""
